id: pm-slack-gmno
title: Consume the canonical attestation gate instead of carrying a copy of it
description: "This repository carried its own 721-line shell scanner and 554-line verifier, duplicated from the same origin as every other package in the fleet. That gate decides whether an artefact may reach the registry, so a false pass is the failure that matters - and the canonical implementation has had many fail-open constructions found and closed in it. A copy frozen at any point in that sequence still admits every construction closed after it. The scanner is deleted, the verifier becomes a thin launcher over the published pm-ops/attestation export, and the changelog-date verifier imports its shell helpers from pm-ops/shell-scan. Measured BEFORE: nonliteral-overwrite,nonliteral-overwrite-cmdsub,bare-brace-scope-escape,subshell-scope-escape,cmdsub-in-command-position,backtick-command-position,unset-after-bind,if-branch-bind,semicolon-same-line-bind (9 wrong). Measured AFTER (target): nonliteral-overwrite,nonliteral-overwrite-cmdsub."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: attestation,security
created_at: "2026-09-07T09:48:14.550Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T09:57:55.539Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-07T09:57:55.520Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-07T09:57:55.520Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Delete scripts/shell-command-scan.ts; Rewrite scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts as a thin launcher over pm-ops/attestation; Repoint scripts/verify-release-changelog-date.ts to pm-ops/shell-scan; Replace test/shell-command-scan.test.ts and test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts as consumer tests; All quality gates pass: check, docstring, coverage, verify:release-publish-attestation, test"
